# DELHIWALA ELEVATION — Architectural Facade & Exterior Execution Rules
# Benchmarked against Studio Lotus & Foster + Partners daylight architectural aesthetic.

## MANDATORY SKILL HOOKS & VALIDATION GATES
- `@ui-ux-pro-max`: Enforce daylight architectural design tokens, 12-column asymmetric grid, zero dark mode, zero gold, 0px border-radius (`rounded-none`).
- `@humanizer`: Ensure 100% of copy reads like an authentic Indian architectural facade & elevation execution partner. Tone is measured, technically precise, and grounded in on-site reality (no marketing fluff, no generic AI phrasing).
- `@test-lab.ai` + `@test` + `/browser`: Run automated accessibility, responsive verification (375px mobile, 1440px desktop), interactive tests, and build validation after every phase.

## CORE DESIGN LAWS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
1. STRICTLY NO DARK MODE: The entire website exists in pristine daylight architectural travertine & warm stone light mode.
2. STRICTLY NO YELLOW / GOLD: All accenting uses warm WPC Teak / Terracotta cladding tone (`#6E473B`) and structural charcoal (`#1C1B19`).
3. ZERO AI TEMPLATE PATTERNS:
   - NO `rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-full` (except technical status dots/avatars). Everything is `rounded-none` (sharp 90-degree architectural cuts).
   - NO floating blurred shadow boxes (`shadow-2xl` with soft spread). Use crisp `1px solid #DCD6CC` hairline borders.
   - NO SaaS icon-in-circle grids or generic cartoonish icons. Use architectural glyphs, Lucide line icons, blueprint coordinate markers, and structural numbering (`01`, `02`, `03`).
   - NO pill badges or gradient tags. Use crisp uppercase monospace tags with hairline borders (`border border-[#DCD6CC] px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] tracking-widest font-mono`).
   - NO broken carousels or uncontrolled sliders. Use structured editorial grid layouts and high-performance interactive horizontal filmstrips or galleries.

## EXACT DAYLIGHT ARCHITECTURAL COLOR PALETTE
- Primary Canvas: `#F6F4F0` (Architectural Travertine / Warm Concrete White)
- Secondary Surface: `#ECE8E1` (Raw Sandstone / Exterior Plaster)
- Primary Ink: `#1C1B19` (Structural Steel Charcoal)
- Muted Notes: `#68635B` (Weathered Stone Grey)
- WPC Timber Accent: `#6E473B` (Warm WPC Teak / Terracotta Cladding)
- Hairline Dividers: `1px solid #DCD6CC`
- Blueprint Focus Lines: `#1C1B19` (Solid architectural frame on focus/active)

## MANDATORY LIBRARIES & INTERACTION PATTERNS
- **Lenis**: Smooth inertial scroll (`lenis` / `lenis/react`) configured at application root for calm, architectural momentum.
- **Animate UI & Vengeance UI**: Staggered editorial text reveals, hairline border expansions, and coordinate grids.
- **Inspira UI & UI Lora**: Architectural hover physics, image scale transforms (`aspect-[16/10]` and `aspect-[4/5]`), technical slide-over drawer for material specs.
- **Forge UI & Uiverse**: Architectural underline form inputs for project estimation, magnetic rectangular CTA buttons with inverted states.

## PHOTOGRAPHY & ASPECT RATIO DISCIPLINE
- All facade and site execution images MUST use `rounded-none`.
- Hero banner & wide elevations: `aspect-[16/10]` or `aspect-[21/9]`.
- Elevation portraits & detail frames: `aspect-[4/5]`.
- Every image frame features a subtle `border border-[#DCD6CC]` with technical location coordinates (`LAT/LONG` or project city).

